{
  "id": "RAN1_P2_CQ1-2",
  "repair_sha256": "7903f18f960a1da17e4e67aebbab4e0d6575d65a8f6718073a0ed6f6272301f9",
  "method": "D",
  "records": [
    {
      "content": "RAN1#100e agreement: If uplink Tx switching is triggered, the length of the additional time for PUSCH preparation procedure equals to the length of UL switching period."
    },
    {
      "content": "RAN1#100e agreement: For SUL, if uplink Tx switching is configured, the state of Tx chains of last UL transmission is assumed in case of no UL transmission."
    },
    {
      "content": "RAN1#100e Working Assumption: For inter-band UL CA, if uplink Tx switching is configured, the state of Tx chains of last UL transmission is assumed in case of no UL transmission. It can be revisited in RAN1#100bis."
    },
    {
      "content": "RAN1#100e agreement (clarified): For standalone SUL, if UL switching period is configured by RRC: The switching period is not always applicable on the carrier configured with switching period; The switching period is only applicable when the scheduled UL transmissions are switched between 1Tx carrier 1 and 2Tx carrier 2; For each UL transmission occasion on a carrier, the existence of the switching period is determined one time every occasion. Note: 2Tx carrier 2 refers to an UL carrier capable of 2 Tx chains and both 1-port and 2-port UL transmissions."
    },
    {
      "content": "RAN1#100e agreement: For inter-band UL CA, if uplink Tx switching is configured, UE is not expected to be scheduled or configured with UL transmissions that result in simultaneous 1Tx transmission on carrier 1 and 2Tx transmission on carrier 2."
    },
    {
      "content": "RAN1#100e Working Assumption: For inter-band UL CA, if option 2 is supported, the following sub-option 2-3 is defined: Minimize RAN1 impact; No new RAN4 impact; No new TDM pattern. It can be revisited in future RAN1 meeting with taking into consideration any relevant RAN4 decisions on DL interruption for UL Tx switching. Option 2-3."
    },
    {
      "content": "RAN1#100e agreement: For inter-band UL CA, if UL switching period is configured by RRC: The switching period is not always applicable on the carrier configured with switching period; The switching period is at least applicable between 1-port transmission in carrier 1 and 2-port transmission in carrier 2."
    },
    {
      "content": "RAN1#100e agreement: For inter-band UL CA, UE is not expected to [be scheduled or configured to] transmit on any of the two carriers in the switching period. FFS: whether to handle the case when switching period cannot be ensured by gNB."
    }
  ],
